- CORRECT AND WORTH KEEPING AS A FACT, independent of J2: THE EVEN-PIXEL GRID. 4:2:0 carries one colour per 2×2 pixels, so a chroma motion vector is the luma one halved — an odd luma offset is a half-pixel chroma offset, which the decoder FILTERS instead of copying. Any exact copy therefore lands on even pixels. This binds the camera drag's snap (under one stage pixel at editor scale) and anything that ever composites by copying. It is the format's limit, not a product compromise.
