- THE THREE-KIND RULE, kept as discipline and not as machinery: every edit is copies of pixels that exist · a small patch of new pixels · new pixels across the frame. It is the right way to say what an edit COSTS before it runs, and J1's chunk invalidation is the same idea at the granularity this product can actually build.
