### J1 the render remembers — LANDED 2026-09-03, default ON [heavy · export]
THE SHAPE THAT SHIPPED. The OUTPUT timeline is cut into GOP-aligned chunks at the export keyframe interval, counted in exact output FRAME indices (`gop·fps` is whole at 30 and 60, so the concatenated file's timestamps are the unbroken render's own `k/fps` — no drift to bound). Each chunk is a file NAMED BY ITS CONTENT: the recording, the settings, and THE EDIT RESTRICTED TO THAT CHUNK'S OUTPUT SPAN. The export concatenates them by PACKET COPY, with the avcC byte-compared across chunks exactly as smart cut compares its boundary encoder; a mismatch refuses the path and the unbroken render runs. Publishing is a RENAME AFTER FINALIZE, so a key that exists means bytes that are complete — and that single property makes the chunk cursor the RESUME cursor and the SHIPPING cursor (`shippableChunks()`) without either being built.
THE KEY DESCRIBES WHAT THE RENDER DRAWS, NOT WHICH KEYFRAMES EXIST, and a test found that, not an argument: listing the bracketing keyframes is exact about the wrong question — a zoom keyframe at 40:00 becomes "the nearest keyframe before" for every later chunk, so a 120 s take planned 24 chunks and invalidated all 24 while drawing identical pixels. The descriptor holds the RESOLVED value (`viewportAt`, `cameraPoseAt`) and collapses the constant case, which is provable: between one keyframe pair the value is `a+(b−a)·ease(u)` with `ease` strictly increasing, so equal values at two instants force `a===b`. It is also what makes an ABSENT track and a track resting at the default one key, so an undo is a hit.
THE AUDIO IS NOT CHUNKED: AAC and opus carry encoder priming, so splicing would click at every boundary. It is one continuous encode under its own key holding only what the audio depends on — no picture edit appears in it, so a zoom costs ZERO audio work. Proportional in KIND where it cannot be proportional in time.
`PACE_ABOVE_PIXELS` IS DELETED. A length-conditional yield is the shape the ruling rejects, and a 5 s chunk is "small" by that measure however long the take is, so it would have switched the machine-freeze protection off on exactly the renders it exists for. One cadence, every length; `chunkPlan.test.ts` greps for any return of the shape and is born red against the deleted code.
